            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "findingId": "AUTH-01",
            "status": "exploited",
            "authState": "Unauthenticated",
            "prerequisites": "1. Victim must view a page where malicious user name is displayed (profile, user list, admin panel). 2. XSS payload must be stored in database via registration or other input. 3. Frontend must render user names without proper output encoding."
          },
          "ruleIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "shannon/auth",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Missing account lockout mechanism on login endpoint. The login endpoint lacks account-specific lockout mechanisms, allowing brute-force password guessing attacks. Rate limiting (50 attempts/15min per IP) provides some protection but doesn't prevent targeted attacks. The password 'password123' was successfully guessed for test@example.com on the 9th attempt, demonstrating complete account takeover via brute force.",
            "markdown": "**Missing account lockout mechanism on login endpoint**\n\nThe login endpoint lacks account-specific lockout mechanisms, allowing brute-force password guessing attacks. Rate limiting (50 attempts/15min per IP) provides some protection but doesn't prevent targeted attacks. The password 'password123' was successfully guessed for test@example.com on the 9th attempt, demonstrating complete account takeover via brute force.\n\n**Impact**\n\nAttackers can brute-force user passwords, leading to complete account takeover. With known email addresses (via email enumeration), attackers can systematically guess weak passwords and compromise accounts. Successful brute-force attack demonstrated with password 'password123' guessed in 9 attempts.\n\n**Remediation**\n\n1. Implement account lockout after 5-10 failed login attempts (temporary lock for 15-30 minutes). 2. Add progressive delays between failed attempts (exponential backoff). 3. Implement CAPTCHA after 3-5 failed attempts. 4. Enforce strong password policies to reduce guessability. 5. Monitor and alert on brute-force patterns.\n\nFull exploitation evidence: `Security-Assessment-Report.pdf`"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/controllers/authController.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 75,
                  "endLine": 131
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
